      "document_hash": "226b539cbf9bfae972ae092499c0d00463de80fd94ff964869995d1f43818b32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-226b539cbf9b-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nDAVID C. FREDERICK, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nCOLLEEN E. R. SINZDAK, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioner.\nJ. SCOTT BALLENGER, ESQUIRE, Washington, D.C.; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "David C. Frederick",
      "case_id": "2021-20-807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "226b539cbf9bfae972ae092499c0d00463de80fd94ff964869995d1f43818b32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-226b539cbf9b-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FREDERICK: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: In 1904, this Court held in Johnson versus Southern Pacific that a motionless dining car was in use when a worker's hand was crushed while he was trying to couple the car with a locomotive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2021-20-807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "226b539cbf9bfae972ae092499c0d00463de80fd94ff964869995d1f43818b32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-226b539cbf9b-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Frederick, you said something or you, in response to the Chief twice, of the functions that a dead locomotive serves in a train like this. I -- I may have read it too quickly, but where is it in the record below? Where are those --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2021-20-807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "226b539cbf9bfae972ae092499c0d00463de80fd94ff964869995d1f43818b32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-226b539cbf9b-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: One final question.\nThe -- you did not mention, in subsection 1 of the LIA, there is the -- it refers --it -- it says that -- it uses the term \"safe to operate.\" What do you make -- that seems to suggest that the purpose of the --of this whole provision is to make sure that use is actually when the locomotive is operative, not when it's non-operative."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2021-20-807",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "226b539cbf9bfae972ae092499c0d00463de80fd94ff964869995d1f43818b32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-226b539cbf9b-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What does that mean, \"placed into service\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice ALITO",
      "case_id": "2021-20-807",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "226b539cbf9bfae972ae092499c0d00463de80fd94ff964869995d1f43818b32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-226b539cbf9b-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 53,
        "start": 53
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What theory of statutory interpretation are you applying?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2021-20-807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "226b539cbf9bfae972ae092499c0d00463de80fd94ff964869995d1f43818b32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-226b539cbf9b-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: So storage,\nthough, if it's on the side track for a few\ndays, you would say it's not in storage unless\nit's been drained of fuel and the battery's been\ndisconnected?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "226b539cbf9bfae972ae092499c0d00463de80fd94ff964869995d1f43818b32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-226b539cbf9b-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: And that something is\nusually unhook the battery, drain the fluid?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "J. Scott Ballenger",
      "case_id": "2021-20-807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "226b539cbf9bfae972ae092499c0d00463de80fd94ff964869995d1f43818b32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-226b539cbf9b-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BALLENGER: Thank you, Mr. Chief\nJustice, and may it please the Court:\nIt seems to me that Petitioner and the\ngovernment are just rewriting the statute that\nCongress wrote. All of this about draining\nfluids and unhooking batteries isn't in the\nstatute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "J. Scott Ballenger",
      "case_id": "2021-20-807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "226b539cbf9bfae972ae092499c0d00463de80fd94ff964869995d1f43818b32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-226b539cbf9b-0003-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 76,
        "start": 76
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. BALLENGER: Absolutely, Your\nHonor. Under the actual regulations, the actual\nregulations say that a dead locomotive movement\nis -- is a movement when the locomotive is not\napplying tractive power, and they explicitly say\nthat the locomotive can be idling."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2021-20-807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "226b539cbf9bfae972ae092499c0d00463de80fd94ff964869995d1f43818b32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-226b539cbf9b-0004-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: -- you acknowledge, don't you, that this statute imposes obligations on the railroads to do things before the train starts moving?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "FRA",
      "case_id": "2021-20-807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "226b539cbf9bfae972ae092499c0d00463de80fd94ff964869995d1f43818b32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-226b539cbf9b-0004-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 96,
        "start": 96
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the FRA's own definition of \"in use\" for purposes of the Safety Appliance Act is in its Mode of Power Compliance Manual and in 49 CFR 232.9, and their definition is that a -- a railcar, including a locomotive, which is a car under the -- the SAA, comes into use when it's -- it's moving or shortly before movement if all inspections have been completed and it's deemed ready for imminent movement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Union Pacific",
      "case_id": "2021-20-807",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "226b539cbf9bfae972ae092499c0d00463de80fd94ff964869995d1f43818b32",
      "evidence_id": "ev-226b539cbf9b-0004-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 98,
        "start": 98
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Union Pacific's operating manual forbids the use of locomotives that are overdue for inspection."
    },
